<problem>
<!-- <title>differentiate product f(x)=exp(x)*quadratic(x)</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="a" from="1" to=" 7" />
<selectFromSequence name="b" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="true" from="-5" to=" 5" />

<math name="answer" simplify="full"> (2*$a *x + $b[1]  + $a *x^2+$b[1] *x+$b[2] )*(e^x)</math>
<math name="fun" simplify="numbers">($a *x^2 + $b[1] *x+$b[2] )* (e^x)</math>
<math name="poly" simplify="numbers">$a *x^2 + $b[1] *x+$b[2] </math>
<math name="exponential" simplify="numbers">e^x</math>
<math name="dpoly" simplify="numbers">2*$a *x+$b[1] </math>
<math name="dexponential" simplify="numbers">$exponential </math>

</setup>


Compute the derivative, <m>\frac{ df }{ dx }</m>, of the function <m>f(x)</m> below

<me>f(x) = $fun .</me>

<m>f'(x) =</m> 
<answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">
<award>$answer </award>
<!-- <award credit='0.9' nSignErrorsMatched="1" feedbackCodes='onesignerror'>$answer </award> -->
<!-- <award credit='0.81' nSignErrorsMatched="2" feedbackCodes='twosignerrors'>$answer </award> -->
</answer>
<!-- <copy prop="feedbacks" tname="answer1" /> -->




<solution>
To calculate the derivative of <m>f(x)=$fun </m>, we need to use the product rule.  The two factors are <m>$poly </m> and <m>$exponential </m>.  By the product rule
<md>
  <mrow>f'(x)\amp = \left($poly \right)' $exponential  + \left($poly \right)\left($exponential \right)'</mrow>
  <mrow>\amp = \left($dpoly \right) $exponential  + \left($poly \right)\left($dexponential \right)</mrow>
  <mrow>\amp = $answer </mrow>
</md>


</solution>


</problem>